2026-02-11 10:51:27,842 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document Zero-Coupon Bond Valuation

A zero-coupon bond makes no annual or semi-annual coupon payments for the duration of the bond. Instead, it is sold at a deep discount to par when issued. The difference between the purchase price and par value is the investor’s interest earned on the bond.

To calculate the value of a zero-coupon bond, we only need to find the present value of the face value. Carrying over from the example above, the value of a zero-coupon bond with a face value of \$1,000, YTM of 3%, and two years to maturity would be $\$1,000 / (1.03)^{2}$, or \$942.59. is relevant
