2026-02-11 10:52:22,844 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document Understanding Operating Revenue

Distinguishing operating revenue from total revenue is important because it provides valuable information about the productivity and profitability of a company's primary business operations.

Despite the fact that operating revenue is recorded separately on financial statements, some firms may attempt to mask decreases in operating revenue by combining it with non-operating revenue. Understanding and identifying the sources of revenue is helpful in assessing the health of a firm and its operations. is relevant
